{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The fear of YHWH is hatred of evil</b> — [Hatred of] evil is in full [form] with a [sheva] naḥ under the mem [of מרע, making it מֵרָע]. And evil is a general term for every deficiency, and a specification from it: pride and arrogance and an evil way and a perverse mouth." "<b>An evil way</b> — an evil conduct." "<b>And a perverse mouth</b> — that turns from matter to matter. And he said: I hated, as though he said, that the fear of YHWH is hatred of these; I too hated them, in the sense of: Do I not hate those who hate You, O YHWH (Psalms 139:21). And the master of the accents [i.e., the Masoretes], who placed a disjunctive accent on the word ופי, did not see this interpretation. And perhaps the word ופי are the words of Wisdom, as though she said: I, Wisdom, dwell with prudence, and I find knowledge of devices, and I knew that the fear of YHWH is hatred of evil and pride and arrogance and an evil way and a mouth — meaning utterance, like: by the mouth of YHWH, and similar, or my agreement and my opinion, like one mouth good to the king (2 Samuel 15:36) — perversity I hated, for wisdom and perversity hate each other, for they cannot stand in one subject." "<b>And perverseness</b> — includes every opponent and every opposite of the good and the upright."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:30.429964509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}